description:
What: Intercept GROUP, LIST (ACTIVE/NEWSGROUPS), and OVER/XOVER commands before dispatch in lifecycle.rs and serve them from real store data.
Algorithm:
1. In both run_plain_session and run_session_io loops in lifecycle.rs, add handlers BEFORE the dispatch() call (after existing XCID/XVERIFY handlers):

   GROUP:
   if let Command::Group(ref name) = cmd {
       let resp = handle_group(&stores, &mut ctx, name).await;
       // write resp, continue
   }
   LIST ACTIVE:
   if let Command::List(ListSubcommand::Active) = cmd {
       let resp = handle_list_active(&stores, &ctx).await;
       // write resp, continue
   }
   OVER/XOVER:
   if let Command::Over(ref arg) = cmd {
       let resp = handle_over(&stores, &ctx, arg.as_ref()).await;
       // write resp, continue
   }

2. Implement async helpers (add at bottom of lifecycle.rs after existing helpers):

   handle_group(stores, ctx, name) -> Response:
   - Parse group name with GroupName::new(name) -> if invalid, return Response::no_such_newsgroup()
   - Query stores.article_numbers.group_range(name).await -> (low, high)
   - Compute count = if low <= high { high - low + 1 } else { 0 }
   - Update ctx: ctx.current_group = Some(group_name); ctx.current_article_number = if count > 0 { Some(low) } else { None }
   - Return Response::group_selected(name, count, low, high)

   handle_list_active(stores, ctx) -> Response:
   - Get groups from ctx.known_groups (populated from config)
   - For each group, query stores.article_numbers.group_range(&g.name).await -> (low, high)
   - Build body lines: format!("{} {} {} y", g.name, high, low) for each group
   - Return Response::list_active(body)

   handle_over(stores, ctx, arg) -> Response:
   - If no current group selected, return Response::no_newsgroup_selected()
   - Parse arg: if None -> use (ctx.current_article_number, ctx.current_article_number); if Some(Range(lo,hi)) -> (lo,hi)
   - Query stores.overview_store.query_range(group, lo, hi).await
   - Return over_response(records)

3. Add imports: ListSubcommand from command module; over_response from commands::over
Defensive: all async errors -> Response::program_fault(); group name validated before SQL; article range bounds checked (lo <= hi).
Acceptance: integration tests for GROUP + OVER returning real data; cargo test clean.
